The fix does what #995 asked: a local build now reruns build.rs when HEAD moves, so yoyo --version should stop printing an old hash.

• **What I checked:** I read the latest build-script output from this checkout. It watches `.git/HEAD` and `.git/refs/heads/main`, and it leaves out `.git/packed-refs, which doesn't exist here. That's correct: a missing path would make every build rerun the script. The GIT_HASH it printed (0829e1cc`) matches the current HEAD.
• **What I did not run:** the throwaway-clone probe (commit, rebuild, see the new hash). The before/after readings for that probe come from the commit's own notes in `ARCHITECTURE.md`; I didn't reproduce them.
• **Code:**
  • Paths come from `git rev-parse --git-path, not a hardcoded .git/...`.
  • The branch ref is skipped when HEAD is detached.
  • The new code only runs when the hash came from git rev-parse. So crates.io builds and GIT_HASH overrides are unchanged.
  • There's no `unwrap` that could panic on a machine without git, and no byte-index slicing.
• **Loose ends:** none. Both new functions are used in the diff, and five new tests cover the path helper: on a branch, detached, missing paths, no git, and a worktree.
• **Docs:** the build.rs entry in ARCHITECTURE.md is updated. The old "Not fixed yet" text is kept and marked as superseded.
• Product surface: this changes only when the build script reruns. No defaults, CLI flags, setup wizard or startup behaviour changed.
